s) rests on a manual measurement in harne8. The spec admits this as a known gap (`:95`), but the trace still marks R2 as satisfied by a test that doesn't reach it.\n- **F2 (low): `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1598`.** This line and `:1631`, `historycheck.go:87`, `report.go:299` and `setup.go:300` run `git status` without `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`. None of them is in the review read view, so this change is unaffected. But the spec's non-goal (`:33`) and residual-risk statement (`:112`) say the existing executors were all checked. The spec's open follow-up, a test that checks every Git executor sets the variable, would catch these.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- **Verified from the code:** the environment is kept, the fix covers every `snapshotGit` caller, and no caller relies on the index refresh.\n- **Unresolved:**\n  - Submodule inheritance is reasoned from Git's behaviour and not tested.\n  - The implementer's statement that the test fails without the variable is not something I could re-run.\n  - The harne8 result (60 errors down to 0) is a manual measurement.\n  - The head mismatch noted above is unexplained.\n- **Accepted risk:** F1 and F2, both low.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-git-status-leaves-the-git-directory-alone.md\",\n      \"line\": 92,\n      \"summary\": \"R2 trace cites TestGitChangedPathsWritesNothingUnderTheGitDirectory, which only exercises R1; R2 (review-check fresh, strict pose check without 'changed during capture') rests on a manual harne8 measurement declared as a known gap.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add an integration test that runs review-check/check under a governed read view on a repository (with a submodule) whose index stat cache is stale, and asserts review.fresh=true with no 'governance read view changed during capture'; retarget the R2 trace to it.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1598,\n      \"summary\": \"git status still runs without GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 in validate.go:1598,1631, historycheck.go:87, report.go:299 and setup.go:300 (via RawHistoryGit/RawGit). They are outside the review read view, so this change is unaffected, but the spec's non-goal and residual-risk text say every existing executor sets the variable.\",\n      \"action\": \"Implement the spec's open follow-up: a test that walks every Git executor of the engine and fails for any that runs status without GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, and set the variable on these callers.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the fix, the gitCommandContext environment build and every snapshotGit caller. Verified: the env is preserved (git_snapshot_integrity.go:576-583, var appended at :113), all snapshotGit callers are covered, and no caller depends on index refresh. Unresolved: submodule children inherit GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS (reasoned from Git's behaviour, not tested); the test failing without the variable was not re-run by me; R2 is a manual harne8 measurement; artifact-check reports head 6e27b06d vs brief 4cc3b954. Accepted: F1, F2 (low).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No shared state, goroutines or lifecycle changed; the fix removes a concurrent writer (index.lock) under .git, which reduces contention with