the exact trigger for git's optional index refresh) and asserts the index is byte-identical and no index.lock remains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-0e2630317d0ecaf3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined D1 against R1: the cause (git status rewriting .git/index via index.lock under a read view watching .git) is removed at its source, matching the policy of the governed executors (governance_read_view_git.go:601, operation_git.go:26). The rejected alternative, filtering .git from observation, would hide real writes. Concluded the design addresses the cause.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the changelog entry, spec and in-code comment at git_snapshot_integrity.go:110-112; they match runtime behaviour. No operational docs or templates are affected.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the error paths: unchanged and typed. The fix eliminates a spurious, non-actionable closeout error (60 in harne8 per the spec).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the diff against the spec's artifact list: the Go change, test, start, changelog and matrix entry are as declared. The derived indexes are regenerated administrative files; artifact-check reports no error for this change. Concluded in scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evide